<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-12--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-12: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.40";
    dc:description "Coverage and polarization are explicit image measurements, and the paper reports both contrasts as significant. The feature table from the confocal cohort was not released. Re-running the group tests requires that table or a new imaging set; the published summary plot is not enough to recompute the differences.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: On the confocal cohort, compare cilia-coverage fraction and a polarization index across the three morphotypes. Morphotype 2 higher on coverage, and morphotype 3 higher on polarization with fewer isolated patches, would support the contrasts; overlapping distributions would refute them.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Cilia masks and the eight indices for the roughly 350 bots are not deposited.", "Polarization and coverage are correlated with size, which also defines the types.", "Significance depends on how the three groups were cut.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.76"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.398"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-12--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2024-anthrobots-12 by Grok 4.7: 0.2";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
